      "review": "The UI writes root.dataset.world before dispatching showcase-world; renderer initializes from that dataset and reconciles model visibility after both models load. Both worlds define background, ink, muted text, accent, secondary, drawer, button, line and dock palette values; focus follows the accent. Renderer changes model visibility and background/floor/light palettes. No gameplay World Shift calls are present."
    },
    "reducedMotion": {
      "status": "PASS_STATIC",
      "review": "Initial page class and OS preference are honored. When reduced motion is active, changes clear active action, reset action diagnostics to idle, disable action buttons and set yaw/lean to zero on rendering frames. Settings changes while reduced motion remains false preserve active actions and their diagnostics. CSS disables nonessential animations and shortens transitions. Render scheduling may continue while visible; no claim of stopped rendering or measured motion is made."
    },
